body:
The controller bit masks here are incorrect (e.g., `PAD_UP = 0x08` is actually START per `NES.PAD`, and `PAD_DOWN = 0x04` is SELECT). This will break cursor movement and any other d-pad logic. Suggest removing these constants and using the built-in `PAD` enum (`PAD.UP/DOWN/START/SELECT`) or correcting the values to match `src/neslib/Enums.cs`.
```suggestion
const byte PAD_UP = 0x10;
const byte PAD_DOWN = 0x20;
```

