body:
Creating a new `ResourceCollectionResolver` instance inside the lambda that executes for each endpoint can be inefficient. The resolver performs the same work (resolving static asset descriptors) for every endpoint that gets created. Consider creating the resolver once outside the lambda and reusing it, similar to how the `ResourceCollectionConvention` pattern works in the existing codebase. This would avoid redundant lookups and improve performance when multiple endpoints are created.
```suggestion
        if (builder is not IEndpointRouteBuilder routeBuilder)
        {
            return builder;
        }

        var resolver = new ResourceCollectionResolver(routeBuilder);

        builder.Add(endpointBuilder =>
        {
            // Check if there's already a resource collection on the metadata
            if (endpointBuilder.Metadata.OfType<ResourceAssetCollection>().Any())
            {
                return;
            }

            // Only add metadata if static assets are registered
            if (!resolver.IsRegistered(manifestPath))
            {
                return;
            }

            var collection = resolver.ResolveResourceCollection(manifestPath);
            var importMap = ImportMapDefinition.FromResourceCollection(collection);

            endpointBuilder.Metadata.Add(collection);
            endpointBuilder.Metadata.Add(new ResourcePreloadCollection(collection));
            endpointBuilder.Metadata.Add(importMap);
        });
```

